  "_comment": "SALVAGE kit: a drum lashed to the hull - an eight-sided tank lying on its side in a pair of crude cradles, with two collar straps over it. External tankage is a raider's tell: nothing is plumbed inside where it belongs. The drum sits off-centre in +X and the straps are at -0.10 and +0.08 rather than symmetric about it, so a run of these does not read as a repeated tile. Long axis Z, so `align: Run` lies it down the surface it is strapped to.",
